// A child in a group of its own starts a grandchild that sleeps, says so, and ends.
// wait then ends the grandchild, with leftovers = kill, the default, or leaves it
// running, with keep.
// The child is tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `start_beat PATH go`: it starts a grandchild that
// makes the file PATH grow for a minute, prints `started` and ends. That the grandchild still
// runs is the file growing in the second after (`beats PATH`), and that it has ended is the
// file no longer growing (`ends PATH`); `stop_beat` ends a grandchild that was left running.
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx

// leftovers = kill
//# make dir kill
//# $ {program} {child} kill kill/file
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| started
//| 0
//# $ {child} ends kill/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| ended

// leftovers = keep
//# make dir keep
//# $ {program} {child} keep keep/file
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| started
//| 0
//# $ {child} beats keep/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| running
//# $ {child} stop_beat keep/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| stopped
